<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Amalia loss rises, gold output to pick up.</title>
<headline>Amalia loss rises, gold output to pick up.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Quarter to end-March versus preceding quarter</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			 4.46 vs 2.09</p>
<p>    Tonnes milled		   3,249 vs  -</p>
<p>    Gold output (kg)		  -   vs 7.18</p>
<p>Full name: Amalia Gold Mining and Exploration Co Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The company commenced commissioning of the carbon-in-pulp secion of the gold recovery plant on February 17 and this was completed by the end of the quarter. Continuous milling operations commenced on April 7 at a rate of 5,000 tonnes a month. This is expected to rise to around 8,000 tonnes towards the end of the current quarter. Gold production currently exceeds 0.6 kg a day and is expected to increase as tonnage and grade improve.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
